// Designed, not tested. Azure Firewall structured logs: connections from snet-fw, with the rule that decided.
// Table and column names depend on the log destination mode (resource-specific or AzureDiagnostics); check current docs.
AZFWNetworkRule
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)
| where SourceIp startswith "10.50.3."
| project TimeGenerated, SourceIp, DestinationIp, DestinationPort, Protocol, Action, Rule
| order by TimeGenerated desc

// NAT gateway and load balancer: use metrics, not logs. In the portal open the resource, Metrics, and chart
//   NAT gateway : SNAT Connection Count (split by Connection State), Dropped Packets, Datapath Availability
//   Load balancer: SNAT Connection Count (split by Connection State), Allocated SNAT Ports, Used SNAT Ports
//   Azure Firewall: SNAT port utilization
